Firstly, the code related to the assert statement has to be surrounded by a try-catch block.

Also, the System.Diagnostics.Debug class should used instead of traditional assertions for this method. Debug.Assert is mainly used to check for conditions that are supposed to never happen during normal execution, such as conditions that will cause invalid operation exceptions or data lost exceptions. 

The correct way to implement it is with the following code:

```cs
void LoadTemplates(string fileName)
{
    try
    {
        // Check if file exists using Debug.Assert
        System.Diagnostics.Debug.Assert(File.Exists(fileName));
    }
    catch(Exception)
    {
        // Handle any unexpected error here
    }
}
```

Please replace `System.Diagnostics.Debug.Assert` with your own debugging methods if you have any, such as `Console.WriteLine`, `Visual Studio Output window`, etc. Also remember that in production environment, don't use assertions for normal run-time checks, they should remain for debugging purpose only.--------------------<code></code>
