void LoadTemplates(string fileName)
{
	bool templatesFileExist = File.Exists(fileName);
	if (templatesFileExist)
	{
		// @@@ the template file exists
        
		// Below is the code that is related to the assert statement "the template file exists"
		string code = @"if (!templatesFileExist)
		{
			throw new FileNotFoundException(""The template file does not exist."");
		}";

		if (!templatesFileExist)
		{
			throw new FileNotFoundException("The template file does not exist.");
		}
	}
}
</pre></code>

In this code, the section of the code under the comment "// Below is the code that is related to the assert statement" represents the actual assertion logic. If you execute this code and the file provided in 'fileName' exists, the assert statement will be true, and you will not see any output. However, if the file does not exist, an FileNotFoundException will be thrown.--------------------The corresponding output assert statements and code comments would be:
