Assert statement:
```cs
Assert.IsTrue(templatesFileExist, "the template file does not exist");
```--------------------Here is the corresponding .cs file:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;

class Program 
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        LoadTemplates("template.txt");
    }

    void LoadTemplates(string fileName)
    {
        bool templatesFileExist = File.Exists(fileName);

        // @@@ the template file exists
        Console.WriteLine("<code>");
        if (templatesFileExist)
        {
            System.Diagnostics.Debug.WriteLine("Assert.IsTrue(templatesFileExist, \"the template file exists\");");
        }
        else
        {
            System.Diagnostics.Debug.WriteLine("Assert.IsFalse(templatesFileExist, \"the template file does not exist\");");
        }
        Console.WriteLine("</code>");
    }
}
```

In this code, we're checking `File.Exists(fileName)` to see if the file at the given file name exists. 

A comment saying "@@@ the template file exists" is followed by the C# code to output the corresponding assert statement to verify that the file actually exists or not.  If the file exists, it outputs "Assert.IsTrue(templatesFileExist, \"the template file exists\")", otherwise it outputs "Assert.IsFalse(templatesFileExist, \"the template file does not exist\")". 

Lastly, the <code> block is closed at the end.--------------------